frr version 8
frr defaults traditional
hostname edge_fw
no ipv6 forwarding
!
router ospf
 passive-interface eth0
 network 203.0.113.0/30 area 0
 network 10.255.255.0/30 area 0
 network 172.16.10.0/24 area 0
 network 10.0.0.0/30 area 0
 network 10.0.0.4/30 area 0
 ! NO 'redistribute static'  : a redistributed static was the original backend
 !   route-leak vector; every advertised prefix is already covered by an explicit
 !   'network' statement above, so nothing legitimate needs redistribution and a
 !   future static (e.g. the edge blackhole for 172.16.20.0/24) will NOT leak.
 ! NO 'redistribute connected': same reason - all connected /30s and /24s on this
 !   device are listed as 'network', so connected redistribution is redundant and
 !   would only risk advertising a future interface by accident.
 default-information originate always
!
line vty
!
